From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:16:32 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] segacd-screen

Sega CD gets its own Screen section, listed after the PC Engine CD and
shown only when the card holds discs. It has the Mega Drive rows.
Shader walks Off and the retro list into Config/segacd_shader.txt; the
in-game Shader row and the shader shortcut walk the same list. Picture
is the Mega Drive picture, Stretch by default, then Actual and 4:3,
stored as segacd in Config/picture.txt, and Stretch follows the live
256 or 320 frame width. PAL Speed plays a European disc at its own
49.70 fps (Native) or at the panel rate (Panel), stored as segacd in
Config/pal_speed.txt. There is no Region row: the core opens the BIOS
the disc's region byte names, and a forced region would boot a disc
under a BIOS slot did not check. None of the rows touches the Mega
Drive choices.
